docs\artifacts-video-script.md:29:> Everything on this Home looks like part of the app. But three of these cards didn't exist in the code yesterday. This subscription radar, this Scalable portfolio card, this savings slider: I asked for them in plain English, and Moneo built them from my real data.
docs\artifacts-video-script.md:115:> Some guardrails: if the model writes a literal date, the save is refused unless I asked for a fixed period, because a literal date freezes the page. Money arrives as exact minor-unit strings and the generated code uses BigInt, never parsing "€1,842.50" back into a float. And AI data scopes are checked again on every view, so if I turn off the AI's access to transactions in Settings, every artifact stops reading them.
docs\artifacts-video-script.md:131:> A real example from preparing this video: I asked for a savings card, and it said "balances unavailable" while the page next to it showed my balance. The cause was that the designer's data sample was cut at 24,000 characters, and a 100-row transaction query came first, so the designer never saw what `balances` looks like and guessed the field names. The fix was to keep the first three items of every list in the sample, so every query's shape fits. Plus a test that fails on the old code.
